WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier and welcome to the Outlast 2 demo.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.960
Now I believe this is the same demo I played in PAX East but

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.040
I have this curse where every time I play a game no matter where I am

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.300
I inevitably find a way to break it and that happened when I was playing this demo

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.220
at PAX. So sorry to the developers and THANK YOU developers for getting me the demo. But either way;

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.600
"You are Blake Langermann, a cameraman working with your wife Lynn.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.320
The two of you are investi-

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.440
[confused mumbling]

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.860
- investigative journalists willing to take risks and dig deeper

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.160
to undercover the stories no one else will dare to touch.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.320
You're following a trail of clues that started with the

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.160
seemingly impossible murder of a pregnant woman known only as

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.120
Jane Doe.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.440
The investigation has led you miles into the Arizona desert,

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.280
to a darkness so deep that no one could shed light upon it,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:51.200
and a corruption so profound that going mad may be the only sane thing to do."

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:51.980
*Slightly disturbing laugh*

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.100
Okay. So I am unbelievab- *woman interrupts Mark*

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.360
[woman's voice over recording] [plane engine whirring]

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.820
[Man's voice, stuttering] Okay! Uh, w-we're good.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.480
[woman's voice (again)]

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.940
*Shit goes down*

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.560
[sounds of panic, alarms beeping, rattling metal]

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.920
[sounds increase]

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.120
*Woman screams*

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:35.420
Mark: 0_0

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.160
Wow.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.000
Yes. I'm very, very excited for this. The subtitles were a little off from the audio there

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.140
but that's okay.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.160
I'm gonna make sure the settings are all good before I get started in to the actual game.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.160
*character grunts*

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.940
[man from recording] "Lynn!"

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:53.860
Lynn?

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.400
Oh there I am.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.720
Oh boy

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.560
Oh God

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.540
Now as far my understanding goes, I don't think that this is the character

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.660
that we're gonna be playing in actually Outlast 2

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.580
of which I am incredibly excited for because Outlast is just

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.020
a shining gem in the horror game genre.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.100
I am super happy not only that is existed but that was amazing.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.920
And even the expansion/DLC or whatever you wanna call it

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.740
Whistleblower, which was also very cool.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.520
So

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.520
Welcome back everybody

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.520
Welcome back to OUTLAST

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.020
*Mark...grunts?*

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.620
You alright, buddy?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.700
Yeah, walk it off.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.200
Rub some dirt in it!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.200
You'll be FIIIIINE...

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.740
Stitch up your broken leg with a few sticks.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:41.760
alright

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.480
Right mouse button as per us[ual]

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.120
and the night vision has returned

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.200
So we just had some sort of uhh...plane accident?

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.600
and this is the husband of

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.560
of the wife, Lynn, that he's calling for

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.880
And that's all

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:57.920
very...

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.420
y'know...

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.120
not happy.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.480
HELLO!

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.260
HI!

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.360
I seem to be in a spot of trouble. Can you help me?

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.300
Please?

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.100
Even though I hear flies in there, somehow.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.540
Yeah, there's probably dead bodies in there...

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.900
I'M AN EXPERT ON KNOWING WHEN DEAD THINGS ARE IN PLACES!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:20.900
And I'm pretty sure...

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.620
If I... zoom in there

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.380
That's PROBABLY blood.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.700
...Probably.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.700
...alright

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.820
I'LL LEAVE YOU ALONE, you seem to be busy.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:30.700
Okay

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.500
Goodbye then!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.020
Alright so like I said before

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.920
I did play this at PAX so I-

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.560
*rustling in the bushes*

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.520
HI!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.400
I don't know if they've changed anything or updated it since then

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.900
I imagine they have because I broke it

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.240
Like I break everything in my life...

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.620
HELLO!?

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.040
Oh that's a pleasant-

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.040
[man's voice] "Is anybody there?"

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.040
Is anybody there?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:56.620
"Please!"

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.040
Please!

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.740
Oh hey, dead guy! I'm whisper yelling!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.740
Thank you, sir!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.260
Have a...

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.460
lovely...

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.320
hey...

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.560
Ugh that's so weird, you can see the flies dusting around

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.480
on his face.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.900
They're just textures that are bouncing around him.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.640
*Mark le gasps*

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.280
Hello...

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:14.940
Hi?

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.100
Oh God damn it I stopped waving the flies away from my face.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:22.080
Now in the demo I didn't take time to explore so that's what I'm trying to do.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:22.900
HI!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.120
[loud thumping]

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.660
Mark: Whoa...

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.100
Oh, so that's how it's gonna be?! A good ol' fashioned knock 'n fight!

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.280
It that actually somebody on the other side of that?

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.920
It's jammed. Hmmmm, what a conundrum we're in.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.420
I guess I'll venture on.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.540
Oh, hi! What the Hell?

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.540
Hey. how's it going there?

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.600
WHO'S THERE?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.380
Uh oh!

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.980
This ain't good

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.260
...What was that?

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:58.420
*distant voice talking in a foreign language*

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.740
Huh?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.700
Say again?

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.700
I don't speak Spanish.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.460
Alright...

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.220
Whoa hi! HEY!

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.460
Dun run away from me...

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.000
Ooh, you gotta mach-ete [pronounced incorrectly]

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.000
Alright..bye buddy...

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.880
I didn't notice these guys before.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.960
[off-camera woman's scream]

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.540
[man's voice] "Jesus."

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.440
I-Is that Lynn? That's not good...

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.380
Hello!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.620
Do you have my wife?

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.800
It's good that there - [laughs] it's good to know that there are family people around here.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.420
[subtle, off-screen voices]

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.060
[voices continue]

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.620
[woman screaming off-screen]

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:36.820
[Markiplier] Ugh.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.540
Ugh.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.020
What is that?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.600
[character makes gagging noises]

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.140
Ugh.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.240
Okay

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.580
Well I seem to be in the thick of trouble.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.280
Okay, so from what I can interpret this- [door slams shut]

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.820
And what I've seen before, this is like a commune

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.880
or s-something way back in the back areas.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.280
Hello?

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.300
I saw you in there.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.160
Oh!

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:58.860
Wow!

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.740
I honestly didn't expect that to open.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.320
...okay.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.960
[excited] Hi buddy! How you doin'?

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.040
You in charge? You seem to have a halo

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.120
but you don't seem like the type of person that deserving of a halo...

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.580
[mumbled] I'll reload the battery in a second.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.940
I just want to make sure that I get to absolutely everything here.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.500
[louder] 'cause I don't want to miss out!

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.860
'Cause I'm -- this is like the -- oh?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:21.400
My God!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.680
What happened here?!

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.960
Ew, gah - why is there a spray?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.600
[disgusted noises]

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.160
I don't wanna know!

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.920
Maybe I should hide in the closet

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.120
but I don't have enough time for that.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.520
We got to go!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.800
We got places to beee.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.940
[quietly] Hello?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.160
Ah.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.140
Is there someone over there?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.080
No? Ok.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:42.400
Alright then.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.520
Ooh, shit.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.500
That's comforting.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.260
Okay.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:50.120
Let me just check this door

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.280
"To open windows"?

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.700
[birds cawing, wings flapping] AH FUCK YOU!

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:55.760
Hi.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.600
Okay. I don't think that was there before

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.560
or maybe it was and I missed out on it.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.420
I don't really know.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.340
Probably did.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:06.280
I apologize if I get jump scared by things that I got scared by already.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.600
Ugh.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.000
Such a big baby.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:11.700
Who is --

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.860
